{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499553-how-can-i-build-a-brawl-character","id":1499553,"title":"How can I build a Brawl character?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-13T11:19:46-08:00","id":1499553,"title":"How can I build a Brawl character?","content":"Lets say the objective is to create a Brawl focused mortal character, one that can leverage the fact they are a competent fighter that is more discrete because they &quot;never carry a weapon&quot; (at least when they can't hide something like a katar or brass knuckles) and is more silent than a firearms user. How could they be built to deal with armor, put up a fight against melee or have enough leeway to close in on a gunslinger? What fighting styles and merits would be most helpful, assuming cross learning via style tags is possible ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T11:36:13-08:00","id":1499555,"title":"","content":"Certain splats are better at this than others. Uratha, for instance, <i>really</i> are <i>perfect</i> for this type of build.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T12:37:26-08:00","id":1499561,"title":"","content":"Depending on the splat brawl is easier than others, but since you specified fighting styles and merits, I'm assuming this is for a mortal character.<br /> <br /> So, first things first, get the Grappling tree (especially if you have hurt locker). Depending on how much brawl a melee user has invested in (when I first started playing, I pumped weaponry and ignored brawl, and now I've learned it's best to have equaling or more brawl dots than weaponry dots), grappling can shut down melee completely or put you in a world of hurt. For stealth you want merits that let you close in faster and have higher speeds, but again grappling can shut down a firearms user.<br /> <br /> Close Quarters Combat can help you with getting into cover faster in a firefight, let you deal lethal damage at the expense of ending a grapple, and it turns the enemies armor against them. So Grappling and CQC really shut down other people. Boxing, Unarmed Defense, and Martial Arts all share tags so you should be able to mix and match those. Street Fighting has always felt a little odd for me since I've never figured out how best to combo it with some of the other fighting merits, but it's there along with the various miscellaneous one or two dot merit maneuvers you can buy that are usually beneficial to grappling. The Police Tactics fighting style also makes your grappling deadlier.<br /> <br /> Anyway, long story short is that Brawl lets you do grappling which absolutely shuts down one character, and that key being one character. As for multiple characters, that's where your unarmed defense and martials comes in since some of those have maneuvers that help in dealing with groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12436-ever-professional","name":"Ever Professional","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12436_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T12:47:14-08:00","id":1499563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499553-how-can-i-build-a-brawl-character?p=1499555#post1499555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Certain splats are better at this than others. Uratha, for instance, <i>really</i> are <i>perfect</i> for this type of build.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is probably the most important context needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T13:36:21-08:00","id":1499572,"title":"","content":"While trying to keep things that apply even beyond the context of character type:<br /> <br /> Beyond grappling being Brawl's real bit deal: anything that boosts Initiative and Speed is also your friend so you can make the most out of Brawl.<br /> <br /> One of the disadvantages of weapons, is that the more damage they do, the more they tend to have Initiative penalties. You want to stack that even more in your favor. Hitting first, esp. with a grappling focus, is key to ensuring you don't take a sword or shotgun to the gut.<br /> <br /> Speed is more of a concern against ranged combatants, but it's the same tactical consideration: if you can reach your opponent, their range advantage stops mattering.<br /> <br /> Stealth and Subterfuge can also be very useful in more &quot;real world&quot; rather than &quot;white room&quot; situations: again, getting close matters, so sneaking up on people, or hiding your violent intentions, can make a lot of difference between getting someone in a choke hold before they know what's going on, or getting stabbed because they readied a knife after they noticed you closing in.<br /> <br /> Whether it's supernatural powers, or Merits, it doesn't really matter how much you can mess people up with Brawl, if you can't get to your opponents quickly, and mess them up before they start in on you. On top of anything that just makes your Brawl stuff that much better, anything that helps get you up close and personal before your enemies can do anything is important.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T13:52:48-08:00","id":1499573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499553-how-can-i-build-a-brawl-character?p=1499563#post1499563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is probably the most important context needed.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case its for a mage character, I want them to be able to complement the speed they get from a Legacy with some mundane skill. As far as I know, there aren't any mage specialized merits for speed or brawl. I am also very curious on how to build a mundane brawler, so I thought asking for a mortal could address both of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ever Professional</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499553-how-can-i-build-a-brawl-character?p=1499561#post1499561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depending on the splat brawl is easier than others, but since you specified fighting styles and merits, I'm assuming this is for a mortal character.<br /> <br /> So, first things first, get the Grappling tree (especially if you have hurt locker). Depending on how much brawl a melee user has invested in (when I first started playing, I pumped weaponry and ignored brawl, and now I've learned it's best to have equaling or more brawl dots than weaponry dots), grappling can shut down melee completely or put you in a world of hurt. For stealth you want merits that let you close in faster and have higher speeds, but again grappling can shut down a firearms user.<br /> <br /> Close Quarters Combat can help you with getting into cover faster in a firefight, let you deal lethal damage at the expense of ending a grapple, and it turns the enemies armor against them. So Grappling and CQC really shut down other people. Boxing, Unarmed Defense, and Martial Arts all share tags so you should be able to mix and match those. Street Fighting has always felt a little odd for me since I've never figured out how best to combo it with some of the other fighting merits, but it's there along with the various miscellaneous one or two dot merit maneuvers you can buy that are usually beneficial to grappling. The Police Tactics fighting style also makes your grappling deadlier.<br /> <br /> Anyway, long story short is that Brawl lets you do grappling which absolutely shuts down one character, and that key being one character. As for multiple characters, that's where your unarmed defense and martials comes in since some of those have maneuvers that help in dealing with groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>So Grappling should be first priority, with Close Quarter Combat a close second and then branch out into striking styles. Any maneuvers I should prioritize obtaining at the start ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-13T13:56:55-08:00","id":1499574,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1499553-how-can-i-build-a-brawl-character?p=1499572#post1499572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While trying to keep things that apply even beyond the context of character type:<br /> <br /> Beyond grappling being Brawl's real bit deal: anything that boosts Initiative and Speed is also your friend so you can make the most out of Brawl.<br /> <br /> One of the disadvantages of weapons, is that the more damage they do, the more they tend to have Initiative penalties. You want to stack that even more in your favor. Hitting first, esp. with a grappling focus, is key to ensuring you don't take a sword or shotgun to the gut.<br /> <br /> Speed is more of a concern against ranged combatants, but it's the same tactical consideration: if you can reach your opponent, their range advantage stops mattering.<br /> <br /> Stealth and Subterfuge can also be very useful in more &quot;real world&quot; rather than &quot;white room&quot; situations: again, getting close matters, so sneaking up on people, or hiding your violent intentions, can make a lot of difference between getting someone in a choke hold before they know what's going on, or getting stabbed because they readied a knife after they noticed you closing in.<br /> <br /> Whether it's supernatural powers, or Merits, it doesn't really matter how much you can mess people up with Brawl, if you can't get to your opponents quickly, and mess them up before they start in on you. On top of anything that just makes your Brawl stuff that much better, anything that helps get you up close and personal before your enemies can do anything is important.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, a brawler who plays it smart always has their weapon at hand. Since their positioning is much more intuitive, they are much more reactive to danger and, once they close in, they can seize the flow of the battle. I imagine it can be terrifying to suddenly discover that is the kind of opponent you are dealing with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T23:47:55-08:00","id":1499724,"title":"","content":"Grappling, even without any fighting styles, is almost always better than straight up Brawl attacks because it forces the opponent's dice pool.<br /> The one downside is the commitment. Once in a grapple, you need to roll to actually get out of it, which can be a problem if the opponent turns out to be an even better grappler, or if your opponents start ganging up on you. In both cases you'd better leave combat asap.<br /> <br /> I very much recommend Clinch Strike from Hurt Locker since it's basically free damage, but otherwise I'd say that maximising your dice pool is more important than any Merits. Pump Strength, Brawl, as many Specialties your ST allows (grappling, chains, fists, claws/teeth, specific manouevres, etc) and Area of Expertise on all those Specs.<br /> A higher dice pool generally ends combat sooner, but in a grapple it also determines which of the characters get to <i>act at all</i>, and an Exceptional basically allows you to <i>act twice</i>. I don't need to state how good that can be.<br /> <br /> In fact, after we realised exactly how bonkers grappling is (even after house ruling it to not be as bad) in our VtR game, my group now has an unspoken agreement not to build grapple focused characters in subsequent campaigns.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-18T10:16:18-08:00","id":1500618,"title":"","content":"Boxing from Hurt Locker maxed out then get yourself the fifth dot from Martial Arts for that plus two damage and you have a good chance of one shotting anyone you fight assuming you punch (technically you could kick) them in the head.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}